# Cogito Mill

Generate and publish long-form agentic reasoning datasets (multi-hop deduction). Stack: Python + uv, LangGraph / Deep Agents, Azure OpenAI + GLM, Hugging Face Hub (`ksopyla/datasets`).

## Projects repositories and links

Repository: https://github.com/meridian21lab/cogito-mill

Organization: https://github.com/meridian21lab

Hugging Face Hubs:
- Krzysztof Sopyla (ksopyla) https://huggingface.co/ksopyla/
- Meridian21Lab — does not have a Hugging Face account yet

## Local environment (uv)

- Package manager: **uv** only (`pip install` / bare `python -m venv` are out of band).
- Create / sync: `uv sync` (uses `.python-version` + `uv.lock`).
- Run tools: `uv run <cmd>` (e.g. `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check`).
- Secrets: copy `.env.example` → `.env` (never commit `.env`).
- Prefer `uv add` / `uv add --dev` over editing `pyproject.toml` by hand.

## Local host CLIs (macOS / Homebrew)

On the developer's Mac these are installed system-wide (`/opt/homebrew/bin`); use them directly — do not reinvent with curl/npx when a CLI fits:

| CLI | Binary | Typical use |
|-----|--------|-------------|
| Hugging Face | `hf` (also `huggingface-cli`) | Hub login, repo create/upload, datasets |
| GitHub | `gh` | PRs, issues, checks, releases |
| Azure | `az` | Azure OpenAI / resource ops, auth |

Auth: `hf auth login` / `HF_TOKEN`, `gh auth login`, `az login`. Prefer env/secrets over interactive login in agents. These are **local-only** — do not assume they exist in Cursor Cloud VMs unless the cloud image installs them.

## Cloud agents (Cursor)

- Image: `.cursor/Dockerfile` (uv + Python 3.12). Install: `scripts/cloud-install.sh` via `.cursor/environment.json` (must stay idempotent).
- Sync: `uv sync --frozen --all-groups`. Run tools with `uv run …`.
- Put API keys in Cursor Cloud **Secrets**, not in the repo: `AZURE_OPENAI_*`, `GLM_*`, `HF_TOKEN`.
- Project skills live under `.agents/skills/`. Prefer `/grill-me`, `/grill-with-docs`, `/to-spec`, `/tdd`, langgraph, huggingface-datasets over inventing one-off skills.
- Do not rely on personal `~/.cursor` rules or marketplace HF plugins in cloud VMs.
- See the Cloud section in `AGENTS.md`; executable setup lives in `.cursor/environment.json`,
  `.cursor/Dockerfile`, and `scripts/cloud-install.sh`.

